<section class="page-head">
  <p class="kicker">A speculative essay &middot; time, transmission, and the one becoming many</p>
  <h1>The One Residue That Travels</h1>
  <p class="lede muted">Suppose every instance of the universe has one Prime Being whose residue can cross
    that instance&rsquo;s depth of time and space &mdash; while every being could occupy the prime role in another
    instance. The residue does not arrive as a preserved personality. It is distributed through minds as
    questions, intuitions and philosophical ideas.</p>
</section>

<section class="wrap narrow reveal">
  <div class="frame frame--first illuminated">
    <p class="kicker">The proposal in one sentence</p>
    <h2 id="t-proposal">One Source Per Universe, Every Being Eligible</h2>
    <p class="lede">Within each universe-instance, only its Prime Being&rsquo;s residue occupies the globally
      transmissible mode. Across different instances, every being could be the one who occupies that role.</p>
    <p><strong>Prime</strong> therefore names a position in a universe, not a superior species, permanent soul
      rank, favoured historical person, ruler, prophet, or author. In this instance, one being&rsquo;s traversal
      establishes the channel through which later subjects inherit. In another instance the boundary
      conditions may select another being. What is unique locally is open modally.</p>
    <p>Let \(u\) label a universe-instance and \(p(u)\) the being occupying its prime role. The residue of
      being \(a\) in that instance is a local trace plus a projection onto that instance&rsquo;s one global carrier:</p>
    <p class="formula">\[
      r_a^{(u)}(x)=r_{a,\mathrm{local}}^{(u)}(x)
      +\delta_{a,p(u)}R^{(u)}(x),
      \qquad
      \sum_a\delta_{a,p(u)}=1.
    \]</p>
    <p>The second relation means <em>one prime role in each instance</em>. The broader possibility is</p>
    <p class="formula">\[
      \forall a\in\mathcal B,
      \qquad
      \Diamond\!\left[p(u)=a\right],
    \]</p>
    <p>where \(\Diamond\) means &ldquo;it is possible in another universe-instance&rdquo;. The formula does not
      prove an ensemble of universes or settle what makes a person the same across possible worlds. It states
      the corrected philosophy: many local residues exist in each world; one becomes globally transmissible
      there; no being is excluded from being prime somewhere. <span class="spec">&#9670;</span></p>
    <p class="muted small">Grading on this page: <span class="sci">&#9670; established physics or
      mathematics</span> &middot; <span class="hist">&#9670; philosophical or historical comparison</span> &middot;
      <span class="spec">&#9670; a conditional mechanism</span> &middot;
      <span class="myth">&#9670; the framework&rsquo;s metaphysical reading</span>.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="wrap">
  <div class="page-head tight">
    <p class="kicker">One role, not one eternally privileged identity</p>
    <h2 id="t-instances">The Prime Being Changes With the Instance</h2>
    <p class="lede muted">The uniqueness condition is horizontal within a world, not vertical across every
      possible world.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="grid three">
    <div class="frame card illuminated">
      <h3>Universe \(u_1\)</h3>
      <p class="formula">\[p(u_1)=A\]</p>
      <p>Being \(A\) occupies the prime role. Its residue is the common carrier in \(u_1\); the residues of
        \(B,C,\ldots\) remain local there.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="frame card">
      <h3>Universe \(u_2\)</h3>
      <p class="formula">\[p(u_2)=B\]</p>
      <p>The assignment changes. A counterpart of \(B\) establishes this instance&rsquo;s channel, while \(A\)
        has no automatic privilege.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="frame card">
      <h3>Universe \(u_3\)</h3>
      <p class="formula">\[p(u_3)=C\]</p>
      <p>A third being can be prime. Nothing in the role itself fixes a proper name; the instance and its
        boundary conditions do the selecting.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="wrap narrow reveal">
  <div class="frame">
    <h3 id="t-counterparts">What &ldquo;the same being elsewhere&rdquo; can mean</h3>
    <p>Possible-world philosophy distinguishes strict identity from counterpart relations. If universes are
      causally separate, there may be no fact that numerically identical \(A\) exists in both. The modest
      reading says that a sufficiently corresponding version of every being could occupy the prime role.
      The stronger reading says one trans-world identity can occupy different roles in different instances.
      This essay needs only the modest reading.</p>
    <p>Nor are the residues of different instances silently pooled. For an instance \(u\),</p>
    <p class="formula">\[
      R^{(u)}:J^+_u(x_{p(u)})\longrightarrow\mathbb R,
      \qquad
      R^{(u)}\not\to R^{(v)}\quad(u\neq v)
    \]</p>
    <p>unless the framework separately supplies a cross-universe portal. One prime per instance therefore
      does not become a noisy choir of every prime inside this universe. <span class="spec">&#9670;</span></p>
  </div>
</section>

<div class="divider">✦</div>

<section class="wrap narrow reveal">
  <div class="frame">
    <p class="kicker">First restraint</p>
    <h2 id="t-relativity">Time Is Not One Universal River</h2>
    <p>Modern physics does not give the cosmos one clock whose &ldquo;now&rdquo; is shared everywhere. Relativity
      assigns each world-line its proper time, and the interval between nearby events depends on the metric:</p>
    <p class="formula">\[
      d\tau^2=-\frac{1}{c^2}g_{\mu\nu}
      \,dx^\mu dx^\nu.
    \]</p>
    <p>Different observers can disagree about the duration and, for spacelike-separated events, even about
      temporal order, while agreeing on the causal structure. <span class="sci">&#9670;</span> A residue that
      moves through time and space must therefore respect light cones unless the proposal openly introduces
      new physics. It cannot simply be everywhere because the word <em>spiritual</em> has been placed beside
      it.</p>
    <p>The philosophical proposal begins after that restraint. Time is treated as the order in which the one
      residue can be <em>received</em>, not as a substance carrying it. Space separates receivers; time makes
      inheritance possible. No later mind receives the source all at once. Each encounters only what can
      reach its event:</p>
    <p class="formula">\[
      x_{p(u)}\prec x_1\prec x_2\prec\cdots,
      \qquad
      R^{(u)}(x_n)=0
      \quad\text{unless}\quad x_n\in J^+_u\!\left(x_{p(u)}\right).
    \]</p>
    <p>The symbol \(J^+_u(x_{p(u)})\) is the causal future of that instance&rsquo;s source event. The mathematics
      belongs to causal geometry; assigning the event to a Prime Being does not. <span class="spec">&#9670;</span></p>
  </div>
</section>

