<section class="wrap narrow reveal">
  <div class="frame illuminated">
    <p class="kicker">The proposed selection rule</p>
    <h2 id="t-only-one">Why Only One Residue in Each Instance?</h2>
    <p>If every being inside one universe possessed an independent globally propagating residue, that
      universe would contain as many common channels as beings. Nothing would explain why their signals do
      not overwrite, cancel or fragment one another. The revised hypothesis keeps one coherent zero-mode per
      instance while allowing the identity of its source to vary between instances.</p>
    <p>Let \(\mathcal P^{(u)}_0\) project residues onto universe \(u\)&rsquo;s coherent mode:</p>
    <p class="formula">\[
      \mathcal P^{(u)}_0r^{(u)}_{p(u)}=R^{(u)},
      \qquad
      \mathcal P^{(u)}_0r^{(u)}_a=0
      \quad\bigl(a\neq p(u)\bigr).
    \]</p>
    <p>The local part is not nothing. It can persist in ordinary matter and memory. It simply has finite reach
      within that instance. The same being whose residue is local in \(u_1\) may be prime in \(u_2\):</p>
    <p class="formula">\[
      \mathcal P^{(u_1)}_0r_A^{(u_1)}=0,
      \qquad
      \mathcal P^{(u_2)}_0r_A^{(u_2)}=R^{(u_2)}.
    \]</p>
    <p>What could enforce one-at-a-time uniqueness? Three possibilities can be imagined: the first traversal
      in each instance creates a topological winding that later traversals cannot duplicate; the selected
      subject occupies that world&rsquo;s non-degenerate ground mode; or the role is fixed by a boundary condition
      rather than by an intrinsic property of the being. These are metaphysical mechanisms, not observations.
      <span class="myth">&#9670;</span></p>
    <p class="lede">Every being is eligible across instances; only one is prime within any particular
      instance. No living person gains authority by declaring which instance this is or claiming to be its
      exclusive mouthpiece.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="wrap narrow reveal">
  <div class="frame">
    <p class="kicker">Transmission without a travelling object</p>
    <h2 id="t-propagation">The Being Does Not Move; the Consequence Does</h2>
    <p>A residue is not the Being packed into a small object and sent forward. It is the change left in the
      conditions from which later events grow. A footprint travels through history without the foot travelling
      with it. A melody crosses centuries while no molecule from the first instrument accompanies the later
      performance.</p>
    <p>If the residue has a physical carrier, causal propagation can be written with a retarded Green
      function:</p>
    <p class="formula">\[
      R^{(u)}(x)=\int_{\mathcal M_u}d^4y\;
      G^{(u)}_{\mathrm{ret}}(x,y)J_{p(u)}(y),
      \qquad
      G^{(u)}_{\mathrm{ret}}(x,y)=0\quad\text{for }x\notin J^+_u(y).
    \]</p>
    <p>This equation says only that effects occur after and within causal reach of their sources inside an
      instance. It does not identify \(J_{p(u)}\), prove that a Prime Being or multiple universes exist, or
      permit faster-than-light thought. If the carrier
      is language, ritual, architecture, genes or recorded media, its path should be historically traceable.
      If it is a new field, that field needs dynamics, coupling strengths and observable consequences. If it
      is purely metaphysical, it should not borrow the authority of a physical equation. <span class="sci">&#9670;</span></p>
    <p>The disciplined form of the idea therefore keeps three levels apart:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Physical transmission:</strong> causal changes in fields, bodies and records.</li>
      <li><strong>Cultural transmission:</strong> words and practices carried between people and generations.</li>
      <li><strong>Metaphysical inheritance:</strong> the conjecture that both are local expressions of one
        prior residue.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>

<div class="divider">✦</div>

<section class="wrap">
  <div class="page-head tight">
    <p class="kicker">How one residue becomes many philosophies</p>
    <h2 id="t-distribution">Distribution Is Interpretation</h2>
    <p class="lede muted">The common residue is not copied into identical minds. It is refracted by different
      bodies, languages, histories and problems.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="grid two">
    <div class="frame card illuminated">
      <h3>The receiving equation</h3>
      <p>Let a mind or culture \(k\) have an interpretive operator \(\mathcal K_k\). Its philosophical
        expression is not the residue alone:</p>
      <p class="formula">\[
        I_k^{(u)}=\mathcal K_k^{(u)}[R^{(u)}]
        +H_k^{(u)}+C_k^{(u)}+\varepsilon_k^{(u)}.
      \]</p>
      <p>Here \(H_k^{(u)}\) is inherited history, \(C_k^{(u)}\) is the immediate material circumstance,
        and \(\varepsilon_k^{(u)}\) includes novelty, accident and error. Even if \(R^{(u)}\) were real, no
        philosophy could be reduced to it.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="frame card">
      <h3>Unity does not require sameness</h3>
      <p class="formula">\[
        I_1\neq I_2\neq\cdots,
        \qquad
        igcap_k	ext{Questions}(I_k)\neq\varnothing.
      \]</p>
      <p>Philosophies can disagree in their answers while repeatedly encountering being, change, identity,
        suffering, causality, unity and multiplicity. The conjecture locates the residue in the recurrence of
        the questions, not in a secret sentence all traditions supposedly share.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="frame card">
      <h3>Diffusion through time</h3>
      <p>A thought moves through citation, translation, rejection and rediscovery. Its distribution can be
        pictured as a branching kernel,</p>
      <p class="formula">\[
        I^{(u)}(x,t)=\int_{-\infty}^{t}dt'\int_{\mathcal M_u}d^3x'\;
        K_u(x,t;x',t')R^{(u)}(x',t'),
      \]</p>
      <p>but the kernel is made of people and institutions, not empty mathematics. Libraries, teachers,
        migrations, prohibitions and technologies determine what survives.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="frame card">
      <h3>No exclusive receiver</h3>
      <p>If one residue is distributed, then possession is the wrong relation. A philosopher can give it a
        form but cannot own the source. Disagreement becomes evidence of different projections rather than a
        licence to declare every difference false.</p>
      <p class="muted">That conclusion is ethical and philosophical, not a theorem.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="wrap narrow reveal">
  <div class="frame">
    <p class="kicker">A family resemblance, not a forced genealogy</p>
    <h2 id="t-traditions">The Same Light Is Not the Same Philosophy</h2>
    <p>Many traditions have names for unity, order or an originating relation: the Greek <em>logos</em>, the
      Dao, Brahman, Spinoza&rsquo;s one substance, process philosophy&rsquo;s becoming, and the recurring contrast
      between the One and the many. <span class="hist">&#9670;</span> These terms are not translations of one
      another. Their histories, practices and arguments differ, sometimes decisively.</p>
    <p>The one-residue conjecture may use them as philosophical prisms: examples of minds asking how plurality
      can arise without becoming absolutely separate. It may not treat resemblance as proof of a hidden
      broadcast. Similar ideas can arise because people inherit one another&rsquo;s texts, because human nervous
      systems face similar conditions, because social problems recur, or by convergence without contact.</p>
    <p class="formula">\[
      	ext{similarity}
      \;\not\Rightarrow\;
      	ext{one supernatural cause}.
    \]</p>
    <p>The stronger and more respectful reading is conditional: <em>if</em> one residue is distributed through
      thought, then philosophy is where that distribution becomes explicit enough to examine itself. Each
      tradition remains a real historical achievement, not a distorted copy of this framework.
      <span class="spec">&#9670;</span></p>
  </div>
</section>

<div class="divider">✦</div>

<section class="wrap narrow reveal">
  <div class="frame illuminated">
    <p class="kicker">Time as inheritance</p>
    <h2 id="t-time">The Present Is a Receiving Edge</h2>
    <p>The past is not physically present as a complete second world available to memory. What is present are
      records: altered states now carrying information about earlier states. A fossil, scar, photograph,
      custom or equation is a current arrangement whose explanation points backwards. <span class="sci">&#9670;</span></p>
    <p>The essay&rsquo;s metaphysical step is to read the durable records inside each instance as partial
      receptions of that instance&rsquo;s one original asymmetry:</p>
    <p class="formula">\[
      	ext{source}
      \longrightarrow
      	ext{trace}
      \longrightarrow
      	ext{interpretation}
      \longrightarrow
      	ext{new trace}.
    \]</p>
    <p>Time then is not what carries a substance away from the source. It is the ordered opening of new sites
      at which the residue can be interpreted and re-inscribed. The future is not already full of the idea;
      it contains conditions under which the idea may acquire another form.</p>
    <p>This also explains why reception is irreversible without claiming that the residue itself creates the
      thermodynamic arrow. Records require entropy-producing processes. Brains metabolise energy; books are
      manufactured; signals dissipate heat. The ordinary arrow makes inheritance materially possible. The
      one-residue proposal supplies a meaning for what is inherited, not a replacement for statistical
      mechanics.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="wrap">
  <div class="page-head tight">
    <p class="kicker">Three readings, in order of increasing risk</p>
    <h2 id="t-ladder">How Much Must Be Believed?</h2>
  </div>
  <div class="grid three">
    <div class="frame card">
      <h3>One &mdash; historical</h3>
      <p>One person or one early event leaves effects that spread through ordinary causal chains. Ideas are
        distributed through speech, texts and institutions. This is common intellectual history and can be
        investigated by evidence.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="frame card">
      <h3>Two &mdash; structural</h3>
      <p>&ldquo;One Prime Being per instance&rdquo; names the shared conditions of minded life in each possible
        world. Similar philosophical questions recur because embodied minds inhabit comparable worlds. No
        cosmic transmitter or literal multiverse is required.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="frame card illuminated">
      <h3>Three &mdash; cosmic residue</h3>
      <p>Each universe-instance selects one actual primordial subject, but every being can occupy that role
        in another instance. Later minds locally receive their own instance&rsquo;s unique coherent mode. This is
        the page&rsquo;s strongest proposal, the closest fit to the Prime Being, and the least supported by evidence.
        <span class="myth">&#9670;</span></p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="wrap narrow reveal">
  <div class="frame">
    <p class="kicker">The objections are part of the proposal</p>
    <h2 id="t-objections">Five Ways the Idea Can Go Wrong</h2>
    <ol>
      <li><strong>The selection problem.</strong> What boundary condition selects one prime in each instance,
        and why exactly one? Moving the role between universes removes permanent privilege but does not yet
        derive the rule.</li>
      <li><strong>The carrier problem.</strong> A physical residue needs an equation of motion and coupling.
        A cultural residue needs a traceable history. A metaphysical residue cannot switch categories whenever
        one account becomes inconvenient.</li>
      <li><strong>The convergence problem.</strong> Shared bodies and recurring social conditions may explain
        recurring philosophical ideas without a primordial subject.</li>
      <li><strong>The plurality problem.</strong> Treating traditions as fragments of one preferred system can
        erase their disagreements and repeat a politics of appropriation. The differences must be preserved.</li>
      <li><strong>The test problem.</strong> If every idea confirms the residue and no possible idea counts
        against it, the cosmic version is an interpretation rather than a testable theory.</li>
    </ol>
    <p class="lede">A philosophy can still matter when it is not physics. It becomes misleading only when it
      hides that difference.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<div class="divider">✦</div>

<section class="wrap narrow reveal">
  <div class="frame">
    <h2 id="t-ledger">Earned, Chosen, Refused</h2>
    <dl class="glossary">
      <dt>Earned</dt>
      <dd>Relativity supplies causal order rather than one universal present. Physical information and
        influence require carriers. Records are present states correlated with earlier states. Philosophical
        ideas demonstrably spread through teaching, texts, translation, institutions and resistance.</dd>
      <dt>Chosen</dt>
      <dd>That every universe-instance has exactly one Prime Being and one globally transmissible residue;
        that every being could occupy the prime role in another instance; that the assignments do not mix
        across worlds without a separate portal; and that recurring philosophical questions are projections
        of each world&rsquo;s residue through different interpretive histories.</dd>
      <dt>Refused</dt>
      <dd>Making one identity eternally prime across every universe. Identifying this instance&rsquo;s Prime Being
        with a living person. Claiming faster-than-light thought. Treating resemblance between traditions as
        proof of one supernatural broadcast. Erasing philosophical differences. Giving any individual
        exclusive authority over the source. Calling metaphor a field equation or a field equation evidence
        for the metaphor.</dd>
    </dl>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="wrap narrow reveal">
  <div class="frame frame--creed">
    <p class="kicker">Closing stance</p>
    <p class="lede">Perhaps one Being&rsquo;s residue travels through each universe&rsquo;s time and space, while every
      being could be that Prime Being in a different instance. What reaches a world is not its source preserved,
      but the possibility of asking again what being means.</p>
    <p>The residue is distributed whenever a mind gives that possibility a form: unity, process, emptiness,
      relation, cause, value, self or world. The forms differ because reception is real work. One source per
      instance does not make one identity supreme across all worlds. Plurality is both between universes, in
      who becomes prime, and within each universe, in how the residue is carried.</p>
    <p class="muted small">Compare the source clock in <a href="/prime-plane/">The Prime Plane</a>, follow
      a residue through <a href="/inverted-toruses/">a universe of inverted tori</a>, examine the physical
      limits of residue language in <a href="/out-of-phase/">The Residue That Did Not Meet Its Opposite</a>,
      and return to the unresolved arrow in <a href="/essays/#t-arrow">Where the Arrow Comes From</a>.</p>
  </div>
</section>
